      "values": []
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "34e5aa3b-db10-40a1-893d-79e98cd3f2f4",
      "key": "02769d5e-74ed-4308-974c-a352334b3445",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Features"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E4* hotel\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHalf board accommodation\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll excursions \u0026amp; guided tours included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlue Badge guide Days 2 to 4\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExecutive coach throughout\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOne free place per 10 paying passengers\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1d09b5af-b95a-4af5-b8f2-323db029e817",
      "key": "545273f5-73de-4300-93dc-512082dafdd7",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Accommodation"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFour nights on half board basis at the centrally located 4* Mercure Hotel in Bridgewater. Facilities at the hotel include a restaurant and bar and all rooms are ensuite.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2d9b0603-29ef-423a-8d3e-d9c039d3d7b1",
      "key": "a5c863b5-ecae-475c-9f94-0302f3439c3b",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELacock Abbey, Fox Talbot Museum \u0026amp; Village\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETyntesfield\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECheddar Gorge\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EGuided tour of Wells\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EGuided tour of Shepton Mallet Prison\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EGuided tour of Sheppy\u2019s House of Cider\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWest Somerset Railway steam train ride\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDyrham Park\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "de535189-b468-4594-8118-f303bac50e3c",
      "key": "ec59a378-48a6-471f-a475-1892283235e9",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tailor your sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EForde Abbey \u0026amp; Gardens - set on the banks of the River Axe, this former Cistercian monastery and its 30 acres of award winning gardens is home to the Mortlake Tapestries, woven from cartoons painted for the Sistine Chapel by Raphael\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETrip along the scenic Tiverton canal - a 90 minute trip on the \u2018Tivertonian\u2019, one of the last remaining horse drawn barges in the UK, offers a truly unique and memorable experience of yesteryear\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMontacute House - a magnificent Elizabethan house with Renaissance features and whose Long Gallery is home to over 50 Tudor and Elizabethan portraits on loan from the National Portrait Gallery and techniques\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Here are some more suggested places of interest you might like to include:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "d7903044-5cb4-487f-8f07-17165c232a1d",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1 \u2013 Lacock Abbey, Fox Talbot Museum and Village\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBoard our private executive coach at your preferred pick up points \u2013 visit a carefully selected National Trust property en route such as Lacock Abbey, Fox Talbot Museum and Village near Bath whose fine abbey, founded in 1232, has survived largely intact and Victorian woodland garden includes an 18th century summer house and rose garden \u2013 check in at the 4* Mercure Hotel in Bridgewater.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2 \u2013 Tyntesfield \u0026amp; Cheddar Gorge\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe National Trust\u2019s Tyntesfield property is an extraordinary Gothic revival extravaganza whose original Victorian interior survives intact and with an unrivalled collection of Victorian decorative arts, an insight into below stairs and a sumptuously decorated private chapel, all surrounded by landscaped gardens, park, farmland and estate buildings \u2013 the cathedral like caves at Cheddar Gorge are million year old Ice Age river beds.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3 \u2013 Wells \u0026amp; Shepton Mallet Prison\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA guided tour of Wells, the smallest city in England, takes in the famous Gothic cathedral with its fine medieval statuary, stained glass, chapter house and astronomical clock, the 13th century Bishop\u0026#39;s Palace and the Vicar\u0026#39;s Close, a complete medieval street \u2013 during a guided tour of the Victorian prison wings, the Hard Labour Yard, the old Gate Lodge and the execution room at Shepton Mallet Prison, the UK\u2019s oldest prison, reveals what life was like for prisoners and officers.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4 \u2013 Sheppy\u2019s House of Cider \u0026amp; West Somerset Railway steam train\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA guided tour and tasting at Sheppy\u2019s House of Cider leads us through more than 200 years and six generations of the Sheppy family making real premium craft cider \u2013 a nostalgic 20 mile steam train excursion from Bishops Lydeard Station to Minehead on the West Somerset Railway through the stunning Somerset countryside and coastline.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5 \u2013 Dyrham Park\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBuilt between 1692 and 1704, the National Trust\u2019s Dyrham Park contains fine textiles and paintings, as well as items of Delftware, reflecting the contemporary taste for Dutch fashions.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Suggested Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Every one of our tours is exclusively for your group and your group alone so each one can be tailor made to suit the interests and profile of your members until you have a tour with an itinerary and at a price which matches the interests and profile of your members."
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "Remember this itinerary is just our suggestion. "
          }
        }
      ]
    },
